    <!-- About screen -->
    <string name="about_tagline">A surround-view dashcam for Zeekr head units: it records the vehicle\'s 360° composite stream and adds playback, a super mirror and more.</string>
    <string name="about_storage_title">About external storage</string>
    <string name="about_storage_body">Recordings are written to external storage only, never to the head unit\'s internal flash — a dashcam writes continuously, and that storage cannot be replaced once worn out.\n\n• The USB drive supplied with the car is enough for basic recording.\n\n• For a higher bitrate or a longer retention window without occupying the original drive, add a second one through the left-hand Type-C port. The head unit picks it up automatically and it can be removed at any time.\n\n• Verified working: a 128 GB USB drive; an NVMe SSD (far faster, which largely removes the write bottleneck, though it runs warmer).\n\n• Optane-based M10 drives are good value, but their capacity is small — roughly the last 20 hours.</string>
    <string name="about_storage_privacy">⚠ Recordings on the USB drive are not encrypted. The drive can be removed and read on any other device, so treat privacy accordingly.</string>
    <string name="about_project_title">Project</string>
    <string name="about_coffee_title">Buy the author a coffee</string>
    <string name="about_coffee_body">PayNow to 9271 6786. Entirely optional; nothing in the app depends on it.</string>
    <string name="about_credits_title">Open source and origins</string>
    <string name="about_credits_evcam">This app is released under the GNU GPL v3.0, inherited from EVCam by suyunkai — the camera, recording and floating-window foundations come from it.</string>
    <string name="about_credits_openavm">That Zeekr head units expose a single pre-composited surround stream (rather than four separate cameras), along with its layout and rendering constraints, was first documented publicly by AVM Recorder by Dantenothing. That project reserves all rights; no code from it has been copied here — only the factual conclusions drawn from its public material. With thanks.</string>
    <string name="about_license_line">Full licence: gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html</string>
    <string name="about_safety_title">Safety notice</string>
    <string name="about_safety_body">Experimental, unofficial software with no affiliation to ZEEKR. While driving, rely on the road itself rather than this app\'s display, and do not assume a recording will always be complete or usable. Use at your own risk.</string>
